  "articleBody": "A fold-down shower seat is a fantastic option for saving space and adding flexibility to your bathroom, but getting the right one installed requires a bit of foresight. You'll definitely want to think about how much wall support is actually needed. These seats really need to be anchored into solid backing, like studs or proper blocking, to be safe and reliable. Don't assume your tile or drywall alone will do the trick! Then, consider how it folds. Will it clear nearby fixtures like your showerhead or controls when it's tucked away? You'll need to measure that clearance carefully. The finished height is also key; many manufacturers recommend 17\"-19\" from the floor for comfortable and accessible use, but always check your local building codes or any specific accessibility requirements you might have. Finally, pay attention to the seat's weight capacity and the quality of its folding mechanism. You want something robust and durable that will last in a wet environment. If you're tackling a new build or a bathroom renovation and need structural backing installed, or if you're dealing with specific accessibility needs, reaching out to a pro like HH Remodeling LLC can make all the difference for a secure and compliant installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
